# Task Research Notes: Project Aegis - AI Agentic Security Hardening Solution

## Research Executed

### File Analysis

- `.github/agents/task-researcher.agent.md`
  - Research specialist agent definition with full toolset access
- `.github/instructions/task-implementation.instructions.md`
  - Implementation standards: progressive tracking in `.copilot-tracking/`, plan-driven development with changes file updates

### Code Search Results

- No existing source code found - greenfield project
- Workspace only contains GitHub agent and instructions configuration files
- Research conducted from authoritative external sources and technology documentation

### External Research

- #fetch:https://www.open-scap.org/
  - OpenSCAP is the de-facto standard open-source framework for security compliance - supports OVAL and XCCDF formats, generates ARF/HTML compliance reports, widely used for CIS/STIG/SRG hardening
- #fetch:https://www.cisecurity.org/cis-benchmarks
  - CIS Benchmarks provide Level 1/Level 2 hardening guidelines in XCCDF + OVAL format, covering OS, network devices, cloud platforms, hypervisors, and middleware
- #fetch:https://public.cyber.mil/stigs/
  - DISA STIGs provided as XCCDF bundles with OVAL evaluation content; SRGs (Security Requirements Guides) are parent documents for STIGs applicable across product families
- #fetch:https://milvus.io/docs
  - Milvus is a cloud-native vector database; supports local deployment via Docker Compose; pymilvus Python SDK for integration; used for semantic similarity search over policy rules and remediation context
- #fetch:https://ollama.com/
  - Ollama runs LLMs locally (Llama 3, Mistral, CodeLlama, etc.); exposes OpenAI-compatible REST API at http://localhost:11434; ideal for air-gapped/private cloud environments
- #fetch:https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/
  - FastAPI is Python async REST framework; native OpenAPI/Swagger docs; WebSocket support for streaming LLM responses; dependency injection for RBAC
- #fetch:https://docs.celeryq.dev/
  - Celery is a distributed task queue for Python; used for async enforcement jobs; supports Redis/RabbitMQ as broker; task chaining for evaluate → remediate → rollback workflows
- #fetch:https://www.ansible.com/
  - Ansible provides agentless SSH-based automation; vast module library for OS, network, storage, VMware, iLO, BIOS; idempotent playbooks; ideal for remediation and rollback implementation
- #fetch:https://docs.paramiko.org/
  - Paramiko is Python SSH library; used for direct SSH connectivity to servers, switches, VMs; supports key-based and password auth; foundation for SSH-based endpoint communication
- #fetch:https://react.dev/
  - React 18 for frontend SPA; hooks-based component model; ideal for HITL code review/editor interface; Monaco Editor integration for rule code editing
- #fetch:https://microsoft.github.io/monaco-editor/
  - Monaco Editor (VS Code editor component) embeds in React; syntax highlighting for Python/Ansible/Shell; ideal for HITL rule implementation review and editing

### Project Conventions

- Standards referenced: Greenfield project - no existing conventions, conventions will be established
