## Key Discoveries

### Project Structure

This is a greenfield AI Agentic application requiring full-stack development. The system has two discrete operational stages:

**Development Stage** (per Solution Type - e.g., PCAI-Small, PCE-Standard):
- Policy ingestion and parsing (OVAL/XCCDF/XML/English-text policies)
- LLM-driven generation of evaluation, remediation, rollback function code per policy rule
- Human-In-The-Loop (HITL) interface for review/edit/approve of generated code
- Service/system selection UI (user chooses which components to harden)
- Saved as a named "Hardening Profile" (unique per Solution Type)

**Enforcement Stage** (per Solution Instance - real deployments with actual IPs/credentials):
- Load a saved Hardening Profile (from Development Stage)
- Upload Solution Instance config JSON (actual endpoints, credentials)
- Execute Evaluation (read-only compliance check)
- Execute Remediation (with Impact Assessment + Dry-Run guard)
- Execute Rollback (undo remediation changes)
- Generate OpenSCAP-compatible compliance reports with graphical dashboard

### Solution Instance Hierarchy (from requirements)

```
Solution Instance
├── RACK-0
│   ├── PDU-00, PDU-01
│   ├── Switch-00, Switch-01, Switch-02
│   ├── Server-00
│   │   ├── iLO-000 (BMC - HTTPS/Redfish API)
│   │   ├── SRController-000 (HPE SR/MR controller)
│   │   ├── BIOS-000 (UEFI BIOS - iLO Redfish)
│   │   ├── hypervisor-000 (VMware ESXi / KVM)
│   │   ├── VM-000, VM-001 (Guest VMs - SSH/HTTPS)
│   ├── Server-01 [similar structure]
│   └── Alletra-10k-00 (Storage - REST API)
└── RACK-1 [similar structure]
```

### Implementation Patterns

**Policy Rule Object Model:**
```python
class PolicyRule:
    rule_id: str           # Unique identifier (e.g., CIS-RHEL-1.1.1)
    title: str
    description: str
    rationale: str
    severity: Literal["critical", "high", "medium", "low", "informational"]
    category: str          # e.g., "filesystem", "network", "authentication"
    target_component: str  # e.g., "iLO", "OS", "Switch", "Hypervisor"
    evaluation_code: str   # LLM-generated Python/Ansible code
    remediation_code: str  # LLM-generated Python/Ansible code
    rollback_code: str     # LLM-generated Python/Ansible code
    status: Literal["pending", "generated", "reviewed", "approved", "rejected"]
    risk_score: float      # 0.0-10.0 for remediation dry-run
    hitl_comments: List[str]
```

**Technology Stack Decision:**

| Layer | Technology | Rationale |
|-------|-----------|-----------|
| Backend API | FastAPI (Python 3.12) | Async, OpenAPI docs, WebSocket for streaming, RBAC injection |
| Task Queue | Celery + Redis | Async enforcement jobs, chaining evaluate→remediate→rollback |
| LLM Runtime | Ollama (local) + LiteLLM | Air-gapped private cloud, OpenAI-compatible API, CodeLlama for code gen |
| Vector Store | MilvusDB (Docker) | Policy rule context, remediation patterns, semantic search |
| Relational DB | PostgreSQL | Workspace, user, policy, solution instance metadata |
| Frontend | React 18 + TypeScript | SPA with HITL code editor, compliance dashboard |
| Code Editor | Monaco Editor | Embedded VS Code editor for rule code review/edit |
| SSH Automation | Paramiko + Ansible | Agentless SSH to servers, switches, VMs |
| BMC/BIOS Access | python-redfish / hpilo | Redfish API for iLO, BIOS, SRController |
| Network Devices | Netmiko / NAPALM | Multi-vendor SSH to Aruba switches |
| Storage Access | REST API clients | HPE Alletra REST API |
| Compliance Engine | OpenSCAP (oscap CLI) | Policy evaluation via OVAL/XCCDF, ARF report generation |
| Reporting | OpenSCAP ARF + React charts | Industry-standard reports + graphical RED/Orange/Green dashboard |
| Containerization | Docker Compose | Local dev; Kubernetes manifests for production |
| Auth | JWT + OAuth2 | Role-based access: Admin, Security Officer, Auditor, User |

