**LLM Code Generation Prompt Pattern:**
```python
RULE_CODE_GEN_PROMPT = """
You are a security hardening expert. Generate Python code for the following security rule.
The code must work with the provided endpoint type and communication protocol.

Rule ID: {rule_id}
Rule Title: {rule_title}
Rule Description: {rule_description}
Target Component Type: {component_type}  # e.g., iLO, RHEL-OS, ArubaSwitch
Communication Protocol: {protocol}       # e.g., SSH, HTTPS/Redfish
Connection Details Template: {connection_template}

Generate three Python functions:
1. evaluate(connection) -> ComplianceResult  # READ-ONLY, returns PASS/FAIL/ERROR + evidence
2. remediate(connection) -> RemediationResult  # Apply the fix, save state for rollback
3. rollback(connection, saved_state) -> RollbackResult  # Restore pre-remediation state

Use paramiko for SSH, requests for HTTPS/REST APIs.
Include error handling and logging.
Return structured results matching the ComplianceResult/RemediationResult/RollbackResult schemas.
"""
```

**OpenSCAP Report Integration:**
```bash
# Generate XCCDF-based evaluation using oscap
oscap xccdf eval \
  --profile xccdf_org.ssgproject.content_profile_cis \
  --results-arf /output/results-arf.xml \
  --report /output/report.html \
  /usr/share/xml/scap/ssg/content/ssg-rhel9-ds.xml
```

**Remediation Impact Assessment - Network Topology Model:**
```python
class ServiceCommunicationChannel:
    source_component: str          # e.g., "kubernetes-node-00"
    target_component: str          # e.g., "vault-service"
    protocol: str                  # e.g., "TLS 1.2", "IPMI", "SSH"
    port: int
    cipher_suites: List[str]
    tls_versions: List[str]
    auth_method: str
    risk_on_hardening: float       # 0.0-10.0 risk score if hardening breaks this channel
```

